{"name":"Dusk in the Valley","hex":"#d2cac8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dusk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to darkness or blackness; moderately dark or black; dusky."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time after the sun has set but when the sky is still lit by sunlight; the evening twilight period.","A darkish colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusk"},{"term":"valley","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elongated depression cast between hills or mountains, often with a river flowing through it.","An area which drains itself into a river."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form the shape of a valley."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dusk","blocks":[{"text":"Dusk occurs at the darkest stage of twilight, or at the very end of astronomical twilight after sunset and just before nightfall. At predusk, during early to intermediate stages of twilight, enough light in the sky under clear conditions may occur to read outdoors without artificial illumination; however, at the end of civil twilight, such lighting is required to read outside. The term dusk usually refers to astronomical dusk, or the darkest part of twilight before night begins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg/330px-Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusk","wikidata":"Q11288132"},{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial ice. These glaciers may remain present in valleys in high mountains or polar areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG/330px-Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley","wikidata":"Q39816"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg/330px-Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg/330px-Scots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScots_pine_at_dusk%2C_Ridley_Plain%2C_New_Forest_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296737.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Dusk_at_the_shore%2C_Silverdale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5042036.jpg/250px-Dusk_at_the_shore%2C_Silverdale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5042036.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Dusk_at_the_shore%2C_Silverdale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5042036.jpg/500px-Dusk_at_the_shore%2C_Silverdale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5042036.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Dusk_at_the_shore%2